    {
      "id": "-ZEdlLo4mL1I7uUSopgPc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -222.85501868749998,
      "y": -156,
      "width": 685.599609375,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1037690383,
      "version": 754,
      "versionNonce": 694975446,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791297963629,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Notes:\n- Always round up (div_ceil). Rounding down silently skips\nthe edges.\n- One edge check per direction: 1D has 1 edge, 2D has 2 edges, \n3D has 3 edges.\n- Same rule each time: one division per direction.\n- Block total stays <= 1024 threads (all three blocks above are 256).\n- Assumes one thread per element. Coarsening / grid-stride loops\n(later) launch fewer blocks.\n- Rule for a thread per element: Choose the block size and\nthen calculate the grid size.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Notes:\n- Always round up (div_ceil). Rounding down silently skips\nthe edges.\n- One edge check per direction: 1D has 1 edge, 2D has 2 edges, \n3D has 3 edges.\n- Same rule each time: one division per direction.\n- Block total stays <= 1024 threads (all three blocks above are 256).\n- Assumes one thread per element. Coarsening / grid-stride loops\n(later) launch fewer blocks.\n- Rule for a thread per element: Choose the block size and\nthen calculate the grid size.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6TyCgNdvw1qX0ORqGPeKs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -213.3250199082031,
      "y": 166.5,
      "width": 666.5396118164062,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1464400655,
      "version": 1841,
      "versionNonce": 2050871690,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791298003872,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The block size is a design choice. It depends on the kernel\nand the hardware, not the data:\na total of at most 1024, a multiple of 32, square if threads\nneed to share neighbors. \n\nThe grid size is arithmetic. Once the block is fixed, \nthe grid follows from the data: ceil(data / block)\nper direction.\n\nSo the order matches the design order:\ndata -> one thread's job -> kernel -> launch shape -> CPU plumbing\n\nThe block belongs to the kernel, and the grid belongs to the launch.\n\nWith gride-stride loops, the grid size is chosen to fit the GPU,\nnot calculated from the data.\n\nCUDA grids and blocks are multidimensional with up to 3 dimensions.\nThe multidimensionality of grids and blocks is useful for organizing\nthreads to be mapped to multidimensional data.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The block size is a design choice. It depends on the kernel\nand the hardware, not the data:\na total of at most 1024, a multiple of 32, square if threads\nneed to share neighbors. \n\nThe grid size is arithmetic. Once the block is fixed, \nthe grid follows from the data: ceil(data / block)\nper direction.\n\nSo the order matches the design order:\ndata -> one thread's job -> kernel -> launch shape -> CPU plumbing\n\nThe block belongs to the kernel, and the grid belongs to the launch.\n\nWith gride-stride loops, the grid size is chosen to fit the GPU,\nnot calculated from the data.\n\nCUDA grids and blocks are multidimensional with up to 3 dimensions.\nThe multidimensionality of grids and blocks is useful for organizing\nthreads to be mapped to multidimensional data.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "gridSize": 20,
    "gridStep": 5,
    "gridModeEnabled": false,
